     1	# O2 Probe PCB — SGX-OX-ROHS-Mini buried compost probe
     2	
     3	## Context
     4	
     5	COMPOST-O2-SENSORS-BUDGET.md selected the SGX-OX-ROHS-Mini (46,20 €, −40…+60 °C,
     6	biased 3-electrode EC cell) as the DIY scale-out cell, conditional on a heated
     7	port: the buried probe conducts heat outward, so every surface otherwise sits
     8	below the dew point of 100 % RH pore gas, and the cell's *continuous* rating is
     9	only 15–90 % RH. This project builds that probe: cell + potentiostat AFE +
    10	closed-loop ΔT heater + environment channels, as a Modbus RTU slave on the
    11	existing farm RS485 bus. First deployment validates against the heated Apogee
    12	reference per the report's first-experiment plan.
    13	
    14	**Decisions locked with Fab:** LMP91000 AFE · probe-side MCU + RS485 Modbus
    15	(4-wire farm convention: brown +12 V, white GND, green A, yellow B) · single
    16	12 V feed (SDI-12-LB supply or PSU; design input 7–15 V) · closed-loop ΔT
    17	heater (~+2 K, PWM) · 2× TMP117 (cell block / surrounding gas) · SHT45-AD1F
    18	(PTFE membrane variant) as a ±3–5 %RH condensation-margin **health channel**,
    19	not a calibrated hygrometer (datasheet: >80 %RH long-term gives ~+3 %RH
    20	standing offset) · **no SCD41** — pore CO₂ (mean ~17.7 %, up to 75 %) pins its
    21	4 % output cap permanently (COMPOST-GAS.md:230); replaced by an **expansion
    22	connector** (12 V, 3.3 V, I2C, spare UART) on the sealed side for a future
    23	SenseAir K33-ICB 0–30 % CO₂ head (51×57 mm module — needs its own housing) ·
    24	DNP barometer footprint (BMP390).
    25	
    26	Project: **`/Users/fab/dev/ee/hw/o2-probe/`** (new dir in the hw repo).
    27	Step 0 of implementation: copy this plan into that dir as `PLAN.md` (global
    28	rule: finalized plans live in the repo).
    29	
    30	## Architecture
    31	
    32	**One elongated 2-layer PCB, two zones split by a potting dam** (routed slot +
    33	silkscreen "POT TO HERE" line). Two-PCB head/body was rejected: an inter-board
    34	connector adds a leakage path exactly where sub-µA integrity matters and
    35	doubles the sealing problem.
    36	
    37	```
    38	[cable]── POTTED ZONE ──────────────────────────────┬─dam─┬── GAS ZONE ─────[tip]
    39	  pads → polyfuse/TVS/rev-pol PFET → buck 12→5 V    │slot │ SGX-OX cell (TH,
    40	  3.3VD LDO → MCU STM32G071 (105 °C), RS485 xcvr    │     │  pins cross the dam)
    41	  3.3VA LDO → 2.5 V VREF → LMP91000 → ADS1115       │     │ SHT45-AD1F (slotted tab)
    42	  LMP91000 hard against dam, RE guard-ringed        │     │ TMP117 #2 (gas, iso tab)
    43	  heater FET (12 V PWM) → 2×2512 resistors on       │     │ DNP BMP390
    44	   cell-block copper island straddling the dam      │     │
    45	  TMP117 #1 on heater island · expansion connector  │     │
    46	```
    47	
    48	- Gas zone: selective conformal coat (apertures clear); cannot be potted.
    49	- Potted zone: potted solid — covers LMP91000, the C/R/W traces, everything
    50	  cable-ward. Potting is also the cable strain relief (no connectors buried).
    51	- **LMP91000 placement:** potted side, <10 mm from cell pins. RE input is
    52	  ~pA-bias; 600 mV across surface contamination at 100 % RH is the dominant
    53	  error source → pot the AFE and traces, guard-ring RE (guard potential
    54	  resolved in Phase 1 from LMP91000 topology; fallback grounded guard), no
    55	  mask relief or vias on the RE trace.
    56	- Heater island: thermally necked from the rest of the board; TMP117 #1 on the
    57	  island closes the PI loop against TMP117 #2 (ΔT ≈ +2 K). ~140 Ω ∥ pair
    58	  → ~1 W ceiling at 12 V.
    59	- tmp117-probe rules carried over: **no I2C pullups on sensed islands; ADD0
    60	  never floats.**
    61	- Tube target: 32 mm OD PVC-U pipe (ID ≈ 28 mm) clears the 14.4 mm cell can;
    62	  board ~20 × 110–130 mm; gas window = slots + ePTFE membrane + mesh
    63	  (enclosure work). Cell faces marked DO NOT OBSTRUCT → copper/part keepouts.
    64	
    65	**I2C map (conflict-checked):** 0x44 SHT45 · **0x48 LMP91000 (fixed)** →
    66	TMP117s at 0x49 (ADD0→V+) / 0x4A (ADD0→SDA) · 0x4B ADS1115 (ADDR→SCL) ·
    67	0x76 DNP BMP390 · 0x68 reserved for K33 on expansion. MENB MCU-controlled.
    68	
    69	**Expansion connector** (replaces SCD41): 8-pin — 12 V, GND, 3V3_D, SDA, SCL,
    70	EXP_INT/GPIO, UART_TX/RX (STM32G071's second USART; degrades to GPIO if pins
    71	run out — K33 speaks I2C anyway). On-board: Molex Micro-Fit 3.0 2×4
    72	(−40…+105 °C) in the potted zone just above the pot line (pad-field fallback
    73	if mated height ~10 mm doesn't clear the tube ID). Enclosure side: second
    74	cable gland or field-sealed M12 8-pin A-coded on the end cap; blanked when
    75	unused. K33 ICB powers from the 12 V pin (it wants 4.5–14 V — verify in
    76	Phase 1). TVS array (TPD4E05-class) + series R on expansion signals; 3V3
    77	expansion budget documented as a hard number (e.g. 200 mA max); I2C bus
    78	capacitance budget for the pigtail recorded in DESIGN.md.
    79	
    80	**ADC:** ADS1115, ratiometric against the same 2.5 V VREF (second channel
    81	reads VREF). 0.07 mA through a ~7–10 kΩ TIA ≈ 0.5 V; 0.1 % O₂ needs ~2 mV
    82	discrimination — MCU-VDD-referenced 12-bit is not enough.
    83	
    84	**MCU:** STM32G071CB, −40…+105 °C grade (ESP32-C3 rejected: 85 °C modules,
    85	radio is dead weight in a buried tube). USART+DE for Modbus RTU. SWD via
    86	TC2030 pads **plus** BOOT0 + UART header for probe-less field reflash.
    87	
    88	**RS485:** THVD1410/SN65HVD72 class (−40…125 °C), external failsafe bias,
    89	DNP 120 Ω termination, SM712 TVS + 10 Ω series on A/B.
    90	
    91	**Power tree:** 12 V → buck 5 V (≥400 mA, fixed ≥600 kHz for filterable
    92	ripple) → 3.3VD (logic/RS485/sensors) and 3.3VA low-noise LDO
    93	(TPS7A20-class: VREF, LMP91000, ADS1115). Bias is continuous whenever 12 V is
    94	present; every cold boot raises SETTLING flag + 15-min timer (datasheet
    95	Note 1).
    96	
    97	## Firmware sketch (register map committed to DESIGN.md)
    98	
    99	Input regs: O2 raw (µA×100) · O2 compensated (%vol×100) · T_cell · T_gas
   100	(0.01 °C) · RH_margin (0.01 %) · EXP data (e.g. K33 CO₂; 0xFFFF = absent) ·
   101	VREF/VOUT diag · pressure (0 if DNP) · heater duty · ΔT target · fault
   102	bitfield · uptime · settle-timer · fw version.
   103	Fault bits: SETTLING (boot, 15 min) · I2C_FAIL per device · HEATER_RUNAWAY ·
   104	VIN_LOW · TEMP_OVER (T_gas > 60 °C, log-only) · DEW_SUSPECT ·
   105	EXP_PRESENT/EXP_FAIL (boot-time auto-probe of reserved addresses).
   106	Holding regs: slave addr, baud, ΔT setpoint, heater max duty, cal constants
   107	(log-linearity K, air-point), SHT45-pulse trigger.
   108	Heater control (revised after review discussion): **primary loop regulates
   109	measured chamber RH** (SHT45, hold ~85–90 % — the actual controlled quantity:
   110	condensation margin + the cell's 90 % continuous-RH spec), with the **ΔT loop
   111	(TMP117 pair) as clamp and fallback** — it takes over when the SHT45 is
   112	faulted, pulsing, or disagreeing with the TMP117s (which is itself a health
   113	signal). TMP117 #2 is specified as *chamber-inlet gas temperature*, not pile
   114	temperature: it is heater-coupled and biased safe-high (dew point is set by
