   116	window, maximally far from the heater island, keeps coupling κ low — the loop
   117	tolerates partial coupling (settles at +2 K/(1−κ)) and only fails near κ≈1
   118	(HEATER_RUNAWAY detects that). 1 Hz PI, ~1 kHz PWM, anti-windup, duty clamp;
   119	safe state = off on sensor fault. SHT45 heater-pulse routine (every 6–12 h + on demand): de-creep plus
   120	dew detection — dry sensor recovers RH quickly post-pulse, wetted sensor shows
   121	the slow-recovery signature → DEW_SUSPECT classifier; pulse + settling window
   122	masked from the RH_margin channel; pulse duty limit per SHT4x datasheet
   123	(exact figure verified in Phase 1).
   124	O₂ compensation: datasheet output-vs-T curve + air-point cal; report raw AND
