The address map checks out as written. The larger architectural problems are elsewhere: the LMP91000’s guaranteed bias-step accuracy does not meet ±10 mV with a fixed 2.5 V reference; the heater loop appears to sense the wrong location if RH is primary; and slave-side RS485 bias must not be populated by default on a shared bus. I’m checking the prior-art implementation rules and doing the thermal/leakage bounds now.
