     1	# tmp117-probe — TMP117 surface probe for shunt-body temperature
     2	
     3	A 9.7 × 15.0 mm two-layer stick that cements to the body of a current shunt and
     4	reports its temperature over I²C on four flying leads. Built for the Riedon PCS
     5	work in `pwr-metering` (`doc/shunt-self-heating.md`), where the fitted TCR is
     6	−10.12 ppm/K and every kelvin of temperature error is 10 ppm of ratio error.
     7	
     8	**Two variants, one set of generators** — see [Variants](#variants):
     9	
    10	| variant | project | outline | mounting |
    11	|---|---|---|---|
    12	| `base` | `tmp117-probe` | 9.7 × 15.0 mm | none — compound and the user's clamp |
    13	| `m3` | `tmp117-probe-m3` | 9.7 × 21.0 mm | M3 (3.2 mm) NPTH on a north tab |
    14	
    15	**Every artefact here is generated.** The generators are the source of truth;
    16	edits made in Eeschema or pcbnew are overwritten on the next run. Close both
    17	before regenerating.
    18	
    19	| file | generates | run with |
    20	|---|---|---|
    21	| `variants.py` | nothing — it is the variant table | either |
    22	| `gen_fp.py` | `lib/tmp117-probe.pretty/*.kicad_mod` | system `python3` |
    23	| `gen_sch.py` | `<variant>.kicad_sch` | system `python3` |
    24	| `gen_pcb.py` | `<variant>.kicad_pcb` | KiCad's bundled `python3` |
    25	| `project_settings.py` | design rules + net classes in `<variant>.kicad_pro` | system `python3` |
    26	| `audit.py` | nothing — it measures | KiCad's bundled `python3` |
    27	
    28	Every generator takes `--variant NAME` and defaults to `base`. An unknown name is
    29	an error, not a silent fallback: a typo that fell through to the default would
    30	rebuild the base board while every line on screen carried the variant's name.
    31	
    32	Regenerate the BOM **without `--group-by`**. Grouping by Value merges R3 and R4
    33	into one row with a DNP field of `no,yes`, which a fab reads as "place both" —
    34	and both fitted shorts SDA to V+ through two 0 Ω links. Caught in review.
