   477	
   478	### How B and C were fixed
   479	
   480	The bottom mask aperture is **three rectangles that merge into one region with a
   481	single notch**, rather than one plain rectangle:
   482	
   483	```
   484	                    A                            y 0.40 .. 3.85
   485	      B   |  keepout: ADD0 B.Cu hop  |  C        y 3.85 .. 6.60
   486	```
   487	
   488	The keep-out is open to the board edge, so it is not an isolated island of solder
   489	mask that could lift — the exported gerber is a single region.
   490	
   491	- **Mask web to the ADD0 hop: 0.175 → 0.325 mm.** `solder_mask_min_width` is now
   492	  0.25 mm (JLCPCB's green minimum) instead of KiCad's default 0.0, and
   493	  `pad_to_mask_clearance` is 0.05 mm — NSMD, which SNOSD82D p.41 marks
   494	  PREFERRED at "0.07 MAX ALL AROUND". Flush mask edges, which 0.0 gives, are
   495	  neither of the two cases TI draws.
   496	### The TPAD via barrels are left open — and why the first fix was wrong
   497	
   498	Review finding C said the six thermal via barrels are open on the contact face.
   499	They were tented for one revision on three arguments. Only one survives:
   500	
   501	- *"Six holes through the insulating barrier"* — **wrong, and it was the argument
   502	  I leaned on hardest.** The barrel is on net `TPAD`, the same net as the pour
   503	  around it, so an open barrel exposes no new potential. And the barrier is the
   504	  TIM between shunt and board; a hole in the **board** does not breach it, it
   505	  only lets compound extrude into it.
   506	- *Solder escaping at reflow* — weak. The nearest paste is 0.30 mm away and not
   507	  in the pads, so little drives wicking.
   508	- *Grease pump-through* — real. Under clamp and thermal cycling, compound
   509	  migrates into six 0.3 mm holes and the bond line thins.
   510	
   511	The cost of tenting, which the first revision did not state: LPI mask stands
   512	10–25 µm proud, so it put a **5.51 mm²** plateau (not the ~3 mm² first written)
   513	about 20 µm high in the middle of a face that must sit flat against a shunt,
   514	directly over the vias — and dropped the contact area to 40.9 mm². With grease
   515	that is roughly neutral. With a solid TIM pad or a hard clamp it holds the board
   516	off the shunt at exactly the wrong place.
   517	
   518	**Decision: leave the barrels bare, no via plugging.** Flat face, full contact
   519	area (**45.9 mm²**), and the accepted cost is grease pump-through over time —
   520	acceptable for a bench probe that gets re-bedded between runs. Resin-filled +
   521	capped vias (IPC-4761 Type VII) would give flat *and* sealed, but only as a
   522	per-order JLCPCB option, which is a dependency that is easy to forget.
   523	
   524	`audit.py::bottom_mask_integrity` was reshaped to match: it gates **foreign-net**
   525	copper exposed in a bottom aperture (finding B) and reports the open TPAD barrels
   526	as a counted, accepted condition. It is not a mute button — a signal via drifting
   527	into the aperture still fails the build, and the guard fails rather than passes if
   528	it has no foreign-net via to measure against.
   529	
   530	**Enabling the rule immediately exposed a second, package-forced case.** At the
   531	TMP117's 0.65 mm pitch the mask dam between the exposed pad and each terminal
   532	land is 0.15 mm, below any fab minimum, so those apertures gang. That is normal
   533	on a fine-pitch no-lead package, and it is handled as a **scoped exemption, not a
   534	muted rule**: `allow_soldermask_bridges` is declared on the TMP117 *footprint*
   535	(it is a property of the package, so the board's copy stays identical to the
   536	library), and `audit.py::mask_bridge_scope` fails the build if any footprint
   537	other than U1 acquires it. The full 0.25 mm dam is still enforced everywhere
   538	else, including every bottom aperture.
   539	
   540	Two harness bugs surfaced while writing the guards, both worth recording:
   541	
   542	- The first `allow_mask_bridges()` used a regex pairing an `(attr …)` line with a
   543	  later `(property "Reference" …)`. Those spanned block boundaries, so the
   544	  exemption landed on **C1** and U1 got nothing — visible only as an unrelated
   545	  `lib_footprint_mismatch` on C1. Now walks balanced blocks and reads both
   546	  fields from inside the same one.
   547	- `bottom_mask_integrity()` first compared aperture bounding boxes in absolute
   548	  page coordinates against via positions in board-local ones. Every via came out
   549	  100 mm from every aperture, so none read as open and none read as close — and
   550	  the guard reported a very comfortable **133 mm of "mask web"**. A wrong answer
   551	  wearing a generous pass. Caught because the injection did not fire.
   552	
   553	### Reviewer claims I checked and did not accept
   554	
   555	- **"6 vias → ~65 K/W"** — the omission was real, the number was not. Measured 34 K/W by walking the copper graph.
   556	- **"contact area 50.2 mm² is 8 % inflated"** — correct in direction; measured 46.5 mm² against the reviewer's 46.29 mm².
   557	- **`_path_length()` is layer-blind** — flagged by inspection only; the reviewer could not build a demonstration and said so. Left open, unconfirmed.
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Independent geometric / thermal audit of one variant's .kicad_pcb.
     3	
     4	Run with KiCad's bundled interpreter:
     5	  /Applications/KiCad/KiCad.app/Contents/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/Current/bin/python3 audit.py
     6	  ... --variant m3   to audit the board with the M3 mounting tab
     7	  ... --calibrate    to inject each defect this file exists to catch and watch it fire
     8	
     9	WHAT THIS IS FOR.  DRC answers "was a rule broken".  Every number DESIGN.md
    10	quotes is a different question, and DRC is not asked any of them:
    11	
    12	  * the exposed-pad-to-terminal-land gap that the TMP117 package forces on us,
    13	  * the copper cross-section of the neck, which is what actually sets how much
    14	    heat leaks from the sensor island to ambient,
    15	  * the exposed contact area on the bottom, and the TIM resistance it implies,
    16	  * the thermal-via count and their series resistance to the exposed pad,
    17	  * the real copper length of each decoupling leg, following track by track,
    18	  * whether any via sits in a pad that gets solder paste.
    19	
    20	Each check FAILS when it cannot evaluate its input.  A check that returns "fine"
    21	because it found nothing to measure is worse than no check: it disappears
    22	exactly when the geometry it guards has been deleted.
    23	"""
    24	
    25	import math
    26	import re
    27	import sys
    28	import pathlib
    29	
    30	try:
    31	    import pcbnew
    32	except ImportError:
    33	    sys.exit("pcbnew not importable -- run with KiCad's bundled python3 (see docstring)")
    34	
    35	HERE = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    36	sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))
    37	import variants   # noqa: E402
    38	
    39	VKEY, V = variants.select()
    40	BOARD = HERE / f"{V['name']}.kicad_pcb"
    41	MOUNT = V["mount"]
    42	Y_TOP = V["y_top"]
    43	KI_FP = pathlib.Path("/Applications/KiCad/KiCad.app/Contents/SharedSupport/footprints")
    44	
    45	# --------------------------------------------------------------- limits and their sources
    46	#
    47	# Every figure below is a DESIGN limit with a stated origin.  None of them is a
    48	# datasheet absolute maximum being used as a pass mark.
    49	#
    50	EP_LAND_GAP_MIN = 0.20      # mm. Package-set (SNOSD82D p.40/41); we must not make it worse.
    51	NECK_LEAK_FRAC_MAX = 0.02   # island->ambient leak as a fraction of island->shunt coupling.
    52	CONTACT_AREA_MIN = 30.0     # mm^2. Bare bottom copper; sets the TIM resistance.
    53	EP_TO_ISLAND_MAX = 80.0     # K/W, exposed pad -> bottom island, copper AND barrels.
    54	                            # Package-limited: the EP land can only be fed by a 1.0 mm
    55	                            # wide strip (SNOSD82D p.40/41), so ~43 K/W of it is not
    56	                            # removable on a rigid 2-layer board. Set above what the
    57	                            # geometry can achieve, not below it.
    58	DECOUPLE_LEG_MAX = 6.0      # mm of copper per leg, U1 pin -> C1 pad.
    59	VIA_TO_PASTE_PAD_MIN = 0.20 # mm. Solder wicks down an open barrel under a paste aperture.
    60	MASK_WEB_MIN = 0.25         # mm. Minimum green solder-mask dam (JLCPCB). This is the
    61	                            # barrier between the bare contact face and the ADD0 hop.
    62	MASK_BRIDGE_EXEMPT = {"U1"} # the ONLY footprint allowed a ganged mask window
    63	
    64	VIA_DRILL = 0.3             # mm, matches gen_pcb.py
    65	THICKNESS = 0.6             # mm, matches the stackup
    66	K_CU = 400.0                # W/m.K
    67	CU_T = 35e-6                # m, 1 oz outer
    68	K_TIM = 1.0                 # W/m.K, ordinary thermally conductive (insulating) compound
    69	TIM_T = 100e-6              # m, assumed bond line
    70	
    71	
    72	def mm(v):
    73	    return pcbnew.ToMM(v)
    74	
    75	
    76	class Audit:
    77	    def __init__(self, board):
    78	        self.board = board
    79	        self.fails = []
    80	        self.lines = []
    81	
    82	    def report(self, name, value, ok, detail):
    83	        self.lines.append(f"  {'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'}  {name:34s} {value:>12s}   {detail}")
    84	        if not ok:
    85	            self.fails.append(name)
    86	
    87	    # ---------------------------------------------------------------- checks
    88	    def ep_land_gap(self):
    89	        """Smallest gap from the exposed-pad land to any terminal land of U1.
    90	
    91	        This is the number DESIGN.md cites as package-set.  If a future edit
    92	        oversizes the EP land, it shrinks here and this fires."""
    93	        fp = next((f for f in self.board.Footprints() if f.GetReference() == "U1"), None)
    94	        if fp is None:
    95	            self.report("EP land gap", "n/a", False, "U1 not on the board -- cannot evaluate")
    96	            return
    97	        pads = {p.GetNumber(): p for p in fp.Pads()}
    98	        ep = pads.get("7")
    99	        others = [p for n, p in pads.items() if n != "7" and n != ""]
   100	        if ep is None or len(others) != 6:
   101	            self.report("EP land gap", "n/a", False,
   102	                        f"expected pad 7 + 6 terminals, found {sorted(pads)}")
   103	            return
   104	        gaps = []
   105	        for p in others:
   106	            gaps.append(self._gap(ep, p))
   107	        g = min(gaps)
   108	        self.report("EP land gap", f"{g:.3f} mm", g >= EP_LAND_GAP_MIN,
   109	                    f">= {EP_LAND_GAP_MIN} mm, {len(gaps)} terminals measured "
   110	                    f"(package-set by SNOSD82D p.40/41)")
   111	
   112	    def _gap(self, a, b):
   113	        """Real shape-to-shape clearance by bisection on Collide()."""
   114	        sa = a.GetEffectiveShape(pcbnew.F_Cu)
   115	        sb = b.GetEffectiveShape(pcbnew.F_Cu)
   116	        if sa.Collide(sb, 0):
   117	            return 0.0
   118	        lo, hi = 0.0, 5.0
   119	        for _ in range(40):
   120	            midv = (lo + hi) / 2
   121	            if sa.Collide(sb, pcbnew.FromMM(midv)):
   122	                hi = midv
   123	            else:
   124	                lo = midv
   125	        return lo
   126	
   127	    def neck_conductance(self):
   128	        """Copper heat leak from the sensor island down the neck.
   129	
   130	        The neck is the dominant conduction path to ambient, and it is copper --
   131	        not laminate -- that dominates it: FR4 at k=0.3 over the 2.4 x 0.6 mm
   132	        neck cross-section carries far less than the traces crossing it do.
   133	
   134	        Measured by intersecting every F.Cu and B.Cu track with a cut line
   135	        across the middle of the neck, so it counts what is ACTUALLY there
   136	        rather than what the generator meant to put there.
   137	        """
   138	        y_cut = 8.5   # mm, mid-neck
   139	        total_w = 0.0
   140	        n = 0
   141	        for t in self.board.Tracks():
   142	            if t.GetClass() != "PCB_TRACK":
   143	                continue
   144	            y1, y2 = mm(t.GetStart().y - ORG.y), mm(t.GetEnd().y - ORG.y)
   145	            x1, x2 = mm(t.GetStart().x - ORG.x), mm(t.GetEnd().x - ORG.x)
   146	            if min(y1, y2) <= y_cut <= max(y1, y2) and abs(x1 - x2) < 1e-6:
   147	                total_w += mm(t.GetWidth())
   148	                n += 1
   149	        if n == 0:
   150	            self.report("neck copper", "n/a", False,
   151	                        f"no track crosses y={y_cut} mm -- either the neck moved or "
   152	                        f"the scan is broken; an empty scan is not a clean scan")
   153	            return
   154	        # The cut only measures the WIDTH.  The conduction path is the whole
   155	        # neck, island edge to wire end.
   156	        length = (NECK_Y - ISLAND_Y) * 1e-3
   157	        g_neck = K_CU * (total_w * 1e-3 * CU_T) / length
   158	        # Compare against how tightly the island is tied to the shunt.  A limit
   159	        # in absolute W/K could be met by lengthening the neck while the contact
   160	        # area shrank; the ratio is the quantity that actually sets the error.
   161	        area, _n = self._mask_area()
   162	        if area <= 0:
   163	            self.report("island leak fraction", "n/a", False,
   164	                        "no bottom mask aperture -- cannot compute the shunt coupling "
   165	                        "this is measured against")
   166	            return
   167	        g_tim = K_TIM * (area * 1e-6) / TIM_T
   168	        frac = g_neck / g_tim
   169	        self.report("island leak fraction", f"{frac * 100:.2f} %",
   170	                    frac <= NECK_LEAK_FRAC_MAX,
   171	                    f"<= {NECK_LEAK_FRAC_MAX * 100:.0f} %; neck {g_neck * 1e3:.2f} mW/K "
   172	                    f"({n} traces, {total_w:.2f} mm wide, {1 / g_neck:.0f} K/W) vs TIM "
   173	                    f"{g_tim * 1e3:.0f} mW/K -- island tracks the shunt to "
   174	                    f"{(1 - frac) * 100:.1f} % of its rise above ambient")
   175	
   176	    def _mask_area(self):
   177	        """Bare TPAD copper: aperture geometry INTERSECTED with the actual B.Cu
   178	        fill, unioned so overlaps cannot double-count.
   179	
   180	        The previous version summed each aperture's bounding box.  That was
   181	        position-blind, copper-blind and overlap-blind: apertures translated
   182	        clean off the island reported the same 50.2 mm2, and twelve stacked
   183	        copies of one 2x2 mm window reported 50.4 mm2 against 4.2 mm2 of real
   184	        bare copper.  Both are the anti-monotone shape -- the geometry gets
   185	        worse and the number does not move."""
   186	        ap = pcbnew.SHAPE_POLY_SET()
   187	        n = 0
   188	        for d in self.board.GetDrawings():
   189	            if d.GetLayer() != pcbnew.B_Mask:
   190	                continue
   191	            bb = d.GetBoundingBox()
   192	            ap.NewOutline()
   193	            for x, y in ((bb.GetLeft(), bb.GetTop()), (bb.GetRight(), bb.GetTop()),
   194	                         (bb.GetRight(), bb.GetBottom()), (bb.GetLeft(), bb.GetBottom())):
   195	                ap.Append(x, y)
   196	            n += 1
   197	        if n == 0:
   198	            return 0.0, 0
   199	        ap.Simplify()
   200	        cu = pcbnew.SHAPE_POLY_SET()
   201	        for z in self.board.Zones():
   202	            if z.GetLayer() == pcbnew.B_Cu and z.GetNetname() == "/TPAD":
   203	                cu.BooleanAdd(z.GetFilledPolysList(pcbnew.B_Cu))
   204	        if cu.OutlineCount() == 0:
   205	            return 0.0, n     # apertures over bare laminate: no thermal contact
   206	        ap.BooleanIntersection(cu)
   207	        return mm(mm(ap.Area())), n
   208	
   209	    def contact_area(self):
   210	        """Bare bottom copper: the actual thermal interface to the shunt."""
   211	        area, n = self._mask_area()
   212	        if n == 0 or area <= 0.0:
   213	            self.report("bottom contact area", f"{area:.1f} mm2", False,
   214	                        f"{n} apertures, but {area:.1f} mm2 of them land on TPAD copper -- "
   215	                        f"an aperture over bare laminate is not a thermal interface")
   216	            return
   217	        r_tim = TIM_T / (K_TIM * area * 1e-6)
   218	        self.report("bottom contact area", f"{area:.1f} mm2", area >= CONTACT_AREA_MIN,
   219	                    f">= {CONTACT_AREA_MIN} mm2; {n} apertures => {r_tim:.1f} K/W through "
   220	                    f"{TIM_T * 1e6:.0f} um of {K_TIM} W/m.K compound")
   221	
   222	    def thermal_vias(self):
   223	        """Resistance from the exposed pad to the bottom island -- MEASURED, not
   224	        inferred from a via count.
   225	
   226	        The previous version counted vias on net /TPAD and reported their barrel
   227	        resistance as if that were the EP-to-island path.  It is not.  The vias
   228	        sit 0.6-1.3 mm NORTH of the exposed-pad land and everything in between
   229	        is a strip of 35 um copper, whose constriction resistance dominates:
   230	        the 1.0 mm wide, 0.6 mm long stub out of the EP land alone is 0.6
   231	        squares at 71.4 K/W per square = 43 K/W, four times the whole via array.
   232	        Counting vias while ignoring the copper that feeds them let a narrowed
   233	        stub degrade the real path ~7x with the guard and DRC both still green.
   234	
   235	        Walks the actual TPAD copper: Dijkstra from the EP land over the track
   236	        graph with edge weight L/(k*w*t), then each via's barrel in series with
   237	        its own copper path, all in parallel.
   238	        """
   239	        import heapq
   240	        R_SQ = 1.0 / (K_CU * CU_T)          # 71.4 K/W per square of 1 oz copper
   241	        ep = None
   242	        for fp in self.board.Footprints():
   243	            if fp.GetReference() != "U1":
   244	                continue
   245	            ep = next((p for p in fp.Pads() if p.GetNumber() == "7"), None)
   246	        vias = [t for t in self.board.Tracks()
   247	                if t.GetClass() == "PCB_VIA" and t.GetNetname() == "/TPAD"]
   248	        segs = [t for t in self.board.Tracks()
   249	                if t.GetClass() == "PCB_TRACK" and t.GetNetname() == "/TPAD"
   250	                and t.GetLayer() == pcbnew.F_Cu]
   251	        if ep is None or not vias or not segs:
   252	            self.report("EP -> island", "n/a", False,
   253	                        f"EP pad {'found' if ep else 'MISSING'}, {len(vias)} vias, "
   254	                        f"{len(segs)} TPAD tracks -- cannot evaluate the thermal path")
   255	            return
   256	
   257	        nodes = {}
   258	
   259	        def nd(pt):
   260	            k = (round(mm(pt.x), 3), round(mm(pt.y), 3))
   261	            return nodes.setdefault(k, [])
   262	
   263	        # Segments must be SPLIT at any via that lands on them.  A via sitting
   264	        # mid-segment is not an endpoint, so an endpoint-only graph silently
   265	        # fails to reach it -- the first version of this check reached 1 via out
   266	        # of 6 and reported a resistance 2x too high.  That was a wrong answer
   267	        # from a partial graph, not a real measurement.
   268	        vpts = [(mm(v.GetPosition().x), mm(v.GetPosition().y)) for v in vias]
   269	        for t in segs:
   270	            a, b = t.GetStart(), t.GetEnd()
   271	            pa = (mm(a.x), mm(a.y))
   272	            pb = (mm(b.x), mm(b.y))
   273	            L = math.dist(pa, pb)
   274	            w = mm(t.GetWidth())
   275	            if w <= 0 or L <= 0:
   276	                continue
   277	            cuts = [0.0, 1.0]
   278	            for vp in vpts:
   279	                # projection parameter of the via onto this segment
   280	                tt = (((vp[0] - pa[0]) * (pb[0] - pa[0]) + (vp[1] - pa[1]) * (pb[1] - pa[1]))
   281	                      / (L * L))
   282	                if 0.0 < tt < 1.0:
   283	                    px = (pa[0] + tt * (pb[0] - pa[0]), pa[1] + tt * (pb[1] - pa[1]))
   284	                    if math.dist(px, vp) <= w / 2 + 0.05:
   285	                        cuts.append(tt)
   286	            cuts = sorted(set(round(c, 6) for c in cuts))
   287	            for t0, t1 in zip(cuts, cuts[1:]):
   288	                q0 = (round(pa[0] + t0 * (pb[0] - pa[0]), 3), round(pa[1] + t0 * (pb[1] - pa[1]), 3))
   289	                q1 = (round(pa[0] + t1 * (pb[0] - pa[0]), 3), round(pa[1] + t1 * (pb[1] - pa[1]), 3))
   290	                r = R_SQ * ((t1 - t0) * L / w)
   291	                nodes.setdefault(q0, []).append((q1, r))
   292	                nodes.setdefault(q1, []).append((q0, r))
   293	
   294	        def nearest(pos):
   295	            pt = (mm(pos.x), mm(pos.y))
   296	            best, bd = None, 1e9
   297	            for n in nodes:
   298	                d = math.dist(pt, n)
   299	                if d < bd:
   300	                    best, bd = n, d
   301	            return best, bd
   302	
   303	        src, ds = nearest(ep.GetPosition())
   304	        if src is None or ds > 1.5:
   305	            self.report("EP -> island", "n/a", False,
   306	                        "no TPAD track starts on the exposed pad -- the pad may be "
   307	                        "connected to nothing; cannot evaluate")
   308	            return
   309	        dist, pq = {}, [(0.0, src)]
   310	        while pq:
   311	            d, u = heapq.heappop(pq)
   312	            if u in dist:
   313	                continue
   314	            dist[u] = d
   315	            for v, w in nodes[u]:
   316	                if v not in dist:
   317	                    heapq.heappush(pq, (d + w, v))
   318	
   319	        drill, wall, thick = VIA_DRILL * 1e-3, 25e-6, THICKNESS * 1e-3
   320	        r_barrel = thick / (K_CU * math.pi * drill * wall)
   321	        g_total, reached = 0.0, 0
   322	        for v in vias:
   323	            n, dd = nearest(v.GetPosition())
   324	            if n is None or dd > 0.4 or n not in dist:
   325	                continue
   326	            g_total += 1.0 / (dist[n] + r_barrel)
   327	            reached += 1
   328	        if reached == 0:
   329	            self.report("EP -> island", "n/a", False,
   330	                        f"none of the {len(vias)} TPAD vias is reachable from the exposed "
   331	                        f"pad through TPAD copper -- cannot evaluate")
   332	            return
   333	        r_total = 1.0 / g_total
   334	        self.report("EP -> island", f"{r_total:.0f} K/W", r_total <= EP_TO_ISLAND_MAX,
   335	                    f"<= {EP_TO_ISLAND_MAX} K/W; {reached}/{len(vias)} vias reached, "
   336	                    f"barrel {r_barrel:.0f} K/W each, copper {R_SQ:.1f} K/W per square. "
   337	                    f"THIS is the down-path, not the via count")
   338	        self._r_down_meas = r_total
   339	
   340	    def decoupling_loop(self):
   341	        """Copper length of each leg of the required bypass loop.
   342	
   343	        SNOSD82D section 9 requires the 100 nF "as close to the supply and ground
   344	        pins as possible".  Measured by walking the actual tracks on each net from
   345	        the U1 pin to the C1 pad -- a pad-to-pin straight line would pass a long
   346	        detour, and centre-to-centre distance measures the wrong property.
   347	        """
   348	        for net, u1pad, c1pad in (("VDD", "5", "1"), ("GND", "2", "2")):
   349	            length = self._path_length(net, ("U1", u1pad), ("C1", c1pad))
   350	            if length is None:
   351	                self.report(f"decoupling leg {net}", "n/a", False,
   352	                            "no connected track path found between the pins -- "
   353	                            "cannot evaluate, so this is a failure, not a pass")
   354	                continue
   355	            self.report(f"decoupling leg {net}", f"{length:.2f} mm",
   356	                        length <= DECOUPLE_LEG_MAX,
   357	                        f"<= {DECOUPLE_LEG_MAX} mm of copper, U1.{u1pad} -> C1.{c1pad}")
   358	
   359	    def _path_length(self, netname, a, b):
   360	        """Shortest track-following path between two pads, in mm, or None."""
   361	        pads = {}
   362	        for fp in self.board.Footprints():
   363	            for p in fp.Pads():
   364	                pads[(fp.GetReference(), p.GetNumber())] = (
   365	                    mm(p.GetPosition().x - ORG.x), mm(p.GetPosition().y - ORG.y))
   366	        if a not in pads or b not in pads:
   367	            return None
   368	        segs = []
   369	        for t in self.board.Tracks():
   370	            if t.GetClass() != "PCB_TRACK" or t.GetNetname() != netname:
   371	                continue
   372	            segs.append(((mm(t.GetStart().x - ORG.x), mm(t.GetStart().y - ORG.y)),
   373	                         (mm(t.GetEnd().x - ORG.x), mm(t.GetEnd().y - ORG.y))))
   374	        if not segs:
   375	            return None
   376	        # Dijkstra over segment endpoints, snapping pads onto the nearest endpoint.
   377	        nodes = {}
   378	        for s in segs:
   379	            for pt in s:
   380	                nodes.setdefault((round(pt[0], 3), round(pt[1], 3)), [])
   381	        for (p, q) in segs:
   382	            d = math.dist(p, q)
   383	            nodes[(round(p[0], 3), round(p[1], 3))].append(((round(q[0], 3), round(q[1], 3)), d))
   384	            nodes[(round(q[0], 3), round(q[1], 3))].append(((round(p[0], 3), round(p[1], 3)), d))
   385	
   386	        def nearest(pt):
   387	            best, bd = None, 1e9
   388	            for n in nodes:
   389	                d = math.dist(pt, n)
   390	                if d < bd:
   391	                    best, bd = n, d
   392	            return best, bd
   393	
   394	        src, ds = nearest(pads[a])
   395	        dst, dd = nearest(pads[b])
   396	        if src is None or dst is None or ds > 0.5 or dd > 0.5:
   397	            return None
   398	        import heapq
   399	        seen, pq = {}, [(0.0, src)]
   400	        while pq:
   401	            d, u = heapq.heappop(pq)
   402	            if u in seen:
   403	                continue
   404	            seen[u] = d
   405	            if u == dst:
   406	                return d + ds + dd
   407	            for v, w in nodes[u]:
   408	                if v not in seen:
   409	                    heapq.heappush(pq, (d + w, v))
   410	        return None
   411	
   412	    def via_in_paste_pad(self):
   413	        """A via under a paste aperture wicks solder out of the joint at reflow.
   414	
   415	        Net-blind on purpose: the real cases are same-net, and DRC does not
   416	        check this at all.  Paste-aware on purpose too: a bare test pad carries
   417	        no paste, so a via beside it cannot wick anything, and flagging it would
   418	        train people to ignore this check.
   419	        """
   420	        vias = [t for t in self.board.Tracks() if t.GetClass() == "PCB_VIA"]
   421	        pasted = []
   422	        for fp in self.board.Footprints():
   423	            for p in fp.Pads():
   424	                if p.IsOnLayer(pcbnew.F_Paste) or p.IsOnLayer(pcbnew.B_Paste):
   425	                    pasted.append((fp.GetReference(), p))
   426	        if not vias or not pasted:
   427	            self.report("via-in-paste-pad", "n/a", False,
   428	                        f"{len(vias)} vias, {len(pasted)} pasted pads -- nothing to "
   429	                        f"compare, so this check verified nothing")
   430	            return
   431	        worst, where = 1e9, ""
   432	        for v in vias:
   433	            for ref, p in pasted:
   434	                g = self._gap_shapes(v, p)
   435	                if g < worst:
   436	                    worst, where = g, f"{ref}.{p.GetNumber()}"
   437	        self.report("via-in-paste-pad", f"{worst:.3f} mm", worst >= VIA_TO_PASTE_PAD_MIN,
   438	                    f">= {VIA_TO_PASTE_PAD_MIN} mm; {len(vias)} vias x {len(pasted)} "
   439	                    f"pasted pads, closest at {where}")
   440	
   441	    def _gap_shapes(self, a, b):
   442	        for layer in (pcbnew.F_Cu, pcbnew.B_Cu):
   443	            try:
   444	                sa = a.GetEffectiveShape(layer)
   445	                sb = b.GetEffectiveShape(layer)
   446	            except Exception:
   447	                continue
   448	            if sa.Collide(sb, 0):
   449	                return 0.0
   450	        sa = a.GetEffectiveShape(pcbnew.F_Cu)
   451	        sb = b.GetEffectiveShape(pcbnew.F_Cu)
   452	        lo, hi = 0.0, 3.0
   453	        for _ in range(40):
   454	            midv = (lo + hi) / 2
   455	            if sa.Collide(sb, pcbnew.FromMM(midv)):
   456	                hi = midv
   457	            else:
   458	                lo = midv
   459	        return lo
   460	
   461	    def die_coupling(self):
   462	        """How much of the shunt's rise above ambient the DIE actually sees.
   463	
   464	        This is the figure that limits a TCR fit, and the board only partly
   465	        controls it.  The die sits between the island (through the exposed pad
   466	        and the thermal vias) and the room (through the package top).  Reported,
   467	        not gated: the dominant term is RthetaJA, which no layout can change --
   468	        it is fixed by insulating the top of the package, and that is a BUILD
   469	        instruction, not a copper one.  See DESIGN.md.
   470	        """
   471	        n = sum(1 for t in self.board.Tracks()
   472	                if t.GetClass() == "PCB_VIA" and t.GetNetname() == "/TPAD")
   473	        if n == 0:
   474	            self.report("die coupling k", "n/a", False,
   475	                        "no thermal vias -- the die/island path cannot be evaluated")
   476	            return
   477	        r_cu = getattr(self, "_r_down_meas", None)
   478	        if r_cu is None:
   479	            self.report("die coupling", "n/a", False,
   480	                        "EP -> island resistance was not measured -- cannot evaluate")
   481	            return
   482	        r_jc_bot = 11.7        # SNOSD82D section 6.4, RthetaJC(bottom), DRV package
   483	        r_down = r_jc_bot + r_cu
   484	        # NOT converted into a k figure any more.  An earlier revision quoted
   485	        # k = 0.76 from RthetaJA / (RthetaJA + down-path).  Two things are wrong
   486	        # with that and they push in opposite directions, so the answer is not
   487	        # trustworthy either way:
   488	        #   * the down-path omitted r_cu entirely (11 K/W instead of ~60),
   489	        #   * RthetaJA is a JEDEC 2s2p board-in-still-air composite that ALREADY
   490	        #     contains a board path, so using it as the parallel die-to-air
   491	        #     branch double-counts the very board this design replaces with a
   492	        #     shunt.  RthetaJC(top) = 82.3 K/W is the conduction term to the case
   493	        #     top, but the convection off ~4 mm2 of package top behind it is tens
   494	        #     of thousands of K/W, which would say k ~ 1.
   495	        # The truthful statement is that the down-path is measurable and the
   496	        # up-path is not, by hand, in this geometry.  Calibrate the built probe.
   497	        self.report("die coupling", f"{r_down:.0f} K/W down", True,
   498	                    f"RthetaJC(bot) {r_jc_bot} + measured copper {r_cu:.0f}. The "
   499	                    f"die-to-AMBIENT branch is NOT modelled here and no k is claimed "
   500	                    f"-- see DESIGN.md. Calibrate the built probe against a reference")
   501	
   502	    def bottom_mask_integrity(self):
   503	        """Two properties of the bottom apertures, both invisible to DRC as shipped.
   504	
   505	        (a) No via barrel may be open on the contact face.  A plated hole there
   506	            pumps thermal compound through the board under clamping load and puts
   507	            a hole through the insulating barrier the isolation argument rests on.
   508	        (b) Every aperture must stand off non-TPAD copper by MASK_WEB_MIN.  DRC's
   509	            solder_mask_bridge only checks whether one aperture spans two nets --
   510	            it says nothing about how THIN the mask web between them is, and with
   511	            m_SolderMaskMinWidth left at KiCad's default 0.0 it could not fire at
   512	            all.  A 0.175 mm web passed a clean DRC before this was written.
   513	        """
   514	        aps = []
   515	        for d in self.board.GetDrawings():
   516	            if d.GetLayer() != pcbnew.B_Mask:
   517	                continue
   518	            bb = d.GetBoundingBox()
   519	            # Board-local, to match the via coordinates below.  Mixing the two
   520	            # frames put every via 100 mm from every aperture, so nothing read as
   521	            # open and nothing read as close -- a wrong answer that looked like a
   522	            # very comfortable pass (133 mm of "mask web").
   523	            aps.append((mm(bb.GetLeft() - ORG.x), mm(bb.GetTop() - ORG.y),
   524	                        mm(bb.GetRight() - ORG.x), mm(bb.GetBottom() - ORG.y)))
   525	        vias = [t for t in self.board.Tracks() if t.GetClass() == "PCB_VIA"]
   526	        if not aps or not vias:
   527	            self.report("bottom mask integrity", "n/a", False,
   528	                        f"{len(aps)} apertures, {len(vias)} vias -- nothing to compare, "
   529	                        f"so this check verified nothing")
   530	            return
   531	
   532	        def gap_to_aps(x, y, r):
   533	            """Distance from a disc to the nearest aperture; negative if inside."""
   534	            best = 1e9
   535	            for (x0, y0, x1, y1) in aps:
   536	                dx = max(x0 - x, 0.0, x - x1)
   537	                dy = max(y0 - y, 0.0, y - y1)
   538	                d = math.hypot(dx, dy) - r
   539	                if x0 <= x <= x1 and y0 <= y <= y1:
   540	                    d = -r
   541	                best = min(best, d)
   542	            return best
   543	
   544	        exposed_tpad, exposed_foreign, worst_web, where = 0, [], 1e9, ""
   545	        for v in vias:
   546	            pos = v.GetPosition()
   547	            x, y = mm(pos.x - ORG.x), mm(pos.y - ORG.y)
   548	            r = mm(v.GetWidth()) / 2.0
   549	            g = gap_to_aps(x, y, r)
   550	            tag = f"{v.GetNetname()}@({x:.2f},{y:.2f})"
   551	            if v.GetNetname() == "/TPAD":
   552	                # Deliberately open -- same net as the pour, so no new potential
   553	                # reaches the contact face.  Counted and reported, never gated.
   554	                if g < 0:
   555	                    exposed_tpad += 1
   556	                continue
   557	            if g < 0:
   558	                exposed_foreign.append(tag)
   559	            elif g < worst_web:
   560	                worst_web, where = g, tag
   561	
   562	        if exposed_foreign:
   563	            self.report("bottom mask integrity", f"{len(exposed_foreign)} exposed", False,
   564	                        f"FOREIGN-net copper bare on the contact face: "
   565	                        f"{', '.join(exposed_foreign[:6])} -- this face is bedded against "
   566	                        f"a shunt in thermal compound")
   567	            return
   568	        if worst_web > 1e8:
   569	            self.report("bottom mask integrity", "n/a", False,
   570	                        "no foreign-net via to measure a mask web against -- the check "
   571	                        "had nothing to evaluate and must not read as a pass")
   572	            return
   573	        ok = worst_web >= MASK_WEB_MIN
   574	        self.report("bottom mask integrity", f"{worst_web:.3f} mm", ok,
   575	                    f">= {MASK_WEB_MIN} mm mask web to the nearest foreign-net via "
   576	                    f"({where}); {exposed_tpad}/{len(vias)} TPAD barrels open by "
   577	                    f"design (accepted: grease pump-through, DESIGN.md)")
   578	
   579	    def mask_bridge_scope(self):
   580	        """A ganged mask window is a package exemption and must stay scoped to it.
   581	
   582	        `allow_soldermask_bridges_in_footprints yes` is board-wide PERMISSION;
   583	        the scope is entirely which footprints declare the attribute.  If that
   584	        set grows, the exemption silently widens and DRC stays green -- an
   585	        exemption that a new part can inherit is a mute button.
   586	        """
   587	        import re as _re
   588	        txt = pathlib.Path(self.board.GetFileName()).read_text()
   589	        have = set()
   590	        for m in _re.finditer(r"\n\t\(footprint ", txt):
   591	            start = txt.index("(", m.start())
   592	            depth, i, in_str, esc = 0, start, False, False
   593	            while i < len(txt):
   594	                c = txt[i]
   595	                if in_str:
   596	                    if esc:
   597	                        esc = False
   598	                    elif c == "\\":
   599	                        esc = True
   600	                    elif c == '"':
   601	                        in_str = False
   602	                else:
   603	                    if c == '"':
   604	                        in_str = True
   605	                    elif c == "(":
   606	                        depth += 1
   607	                    elif c == ")":
   608	                        depth -= 1
   609	                        if depth == 0:
   610	                            break
   611	                i += 1
   612	            blk = txt[start:i + 1]
   613	            r = _re.search(r'\(property "Reference" "([^"]+)"', blk)
   614	            a = _re.search(r"\(attr ([^\)]*)\)", blk)
   615	            if r and a and "allow_soldermask_bridges" in a.group(1):
   616	                have.add(r.group(1))
   617	        mw = _re.search(r"\(solder_mask_min_width ([\d.]+)\)", txt)
   618	        width = float(mw.group(1)) if mw else 0.0
   619	        ok = have == MASK_BRIDGE_EXEMPT and width >= MASK_WEB_MIN
   620	        self.report("mask-bridge scope", f"{sorted(have) or 'none'}", ok,
   621	                    f"must be exactly {sorted(MASK_BRIDGE_EXEMPT)} (package-forced at "
   622	                    f"0.65 mm pitch); solder_mask_min_width = {width} mm, needs "
   623	                    f">= {MASK_WEB_MIN} -- a zero constraint disables the rule as "
   624	                    f"completely as severity 'ignore' does")
   625	
   626	    def stackup_present(self):
   627	        """Board thickness and finish, READ rather than grepped for.
   628	
   629	        The previous version tested `'(stackup' in txt and '(copper_finish
   630	        "ENIG")' in txt` and printed "0.6 mm, 2 layer, ENIG" -- a presence proxy
   631	        whose detail string asserted a number the code never looked at.  It
   632	        passed a board carrying `(general (thickness 1.6))`, which is the field
   633	        kicad-cli copies into the .gbrjob as BoardThickness and therefore the
   634	        one the fab builds to.  Every 0.6 mm-dependent figure here was unbacked.
   635	        """
   636	        import re as _re
   637	        txt = pathlib.Path(self.board.GetFileName()).read_text()
   638	        want = 0.6
   639	        m = _re.search(r"\(general\s*\(thickness ([\d.]+)\)", txt)
   640	        if not m:
   641	            self.report("stackup", "n/a", False,
   642	                        "no (general (thickness ...)) -- the fab would be told nothing")
   643	            return
   644	        declared = float(m.group(1))
   645	        block = _re.search(r"\(stackup(.*?)\n\t\t\)", txt, _re.S)
   646	        if not block:
   647	            self.report("stackup", "n/a", False,
   648	                        "no (stackup ...) block -- the fab builds its house stack and "
   649	                        "every dielectric-dependent number here is unbacked")
   650	            return
   651	        layers = sum(float(v) for v in _re.findall(r"\(thickness ([\d.]+)\)", block.group(1)))
   652	        finish = "ENIG" if '(copper_finish "ENIG")' in block.group(1) else "?"
   653	        n_cu = block.group(1).count('(type "copper")')
   654	        ok = (abs(declared - want) < 0.01 and abs(layers - declared) < 0.05
   655	              and finish == "ENIG" and n_cu == 2)
   656	        self.report("stackup", f"{declared:.2f} mm", ok,
   657	                    f"want {want} mm; stackup layers sum to {layers:.3f} mm, "
   658	                    f"{n_cu} copper layers, finish {finish}. The declared thickness is "
   659	                    f"what reaches the fab via .gbrjob BoardThickness")
   660	
   661	    # ------------------------------------------------- mounting hardware (m3 variant)
   662	    def _hole_centre(self):
   663	        """Centre of the board's ONE unplated hole, or None.
   664	
   665	        Read off the board, never from variants.py.  The first version of this
   666	        took the coordinates from the table, so the two checks below measured
   667	        clearance and seating at the place the hole was SUPPOSED to be: sliding
   668	        the real hole 2.5 mm into the thermal copper left both of them reporting
   669	        the original, comfortable numbers.  A guard that evaluates the spec
   670	        instead of the artefact cannot see the artefact drift away from it.
   671	        """
   672	        holes = [p for fp in self.board.Footprints() for p in fp.Pads()
   673	                 if p.GetAttribute() == pcbnew.PAD_ATTRIB_NPTH]
   674	        return holes[0].GetPosition() if len(holes) == 1 else None
   675	
   676	    def mounting_hardware(self):
   677	        """The unplated holes on the board must be exactly what the variant asks for.
   678	
   679	        Runs on BOTH variants, and that is deliberate.  On `base` it asserts
   680	        ZERO unplated holes: a check that only exists when the feature exists
   681	        cannot notice the feature appearing where it should not be, and a stray
   682	        mounting hole is the kind of thing a copy-paste puts on a board.
   683	        """
   684	        holes = [(fp.GetReference(), p) for fp in self.board.Footprints()
   685	                 for p in fp.Pads() if p.GetAttribute() == pcbnew.PAD_ATTRIB_NPTH]
   686	        want = 1 if MOUNT else 0
   687	        if len(holes) != want:
   688	            self.report("M3 hole", f"{len(holes)} NPTH", False,
   689	                        f"variant {VKEY!r} specifies exactly {want} unplated hole(s); "
   690	                        f"found {[r for r, _ in holes]}")
   691	            return
   692	        if not MOUNT:
   693	            self.report("M3 hole", "none", True,
   694	                        f"variant {VKEY!r} carries no mounting hardware, and the board "
   695	                        f"has no unplated holes on it")
   696	            return
   697	        ref, p = holes[0]
   698	        drill = (mm(p.GetDrillSize().x), mm(p.GetDrillSize().y))
   699	        size = (mm(p.GetSize().x), mm(p.GetSize().y))
   700	        pos = p.GetPosition()
   701	        xy = (mm(pos.x - ORG.x), mm(pos.y - ORG.y))
   702	        # size == drill is how "no annular ring, no copper" is expressed in the
   703	        # file format.  An NPTH pad whose copper is larger than its drill would
   704	        # put a copper washer under the screw head -- the exact thing the
   705	        # keep-out below exists to prevent, arriving from the other direction.
   706	        bad = []
   707	        if ref != MOUNT["ref"]:
   708	            bad.append(f"reference {ref}, want {MOUNT['ref']}")
   709	        if abs(drill[0] - MOUNT["drill"]) > 5e-4 or abs(drill[1] - drill[0]) > 5e-4:
   710	            bad.append(f"drill {drill[0]:.3f} x {drill[1]:.3f}, want "
   711	                       f"{MOUNT['drill']} round")
   712	        if abs(size[0] - drill[0]) > 5e-4 or abs(size[1] - drill[1]) > 5e-4:
   713	            bad.append(f"pad copper {size[0]:.3f} x {size[1]:.3f} is larger than the "
   714	                       f"drill -- that is an annular ring under the screw head")
   715	        if abs(xy[0] - MOUNT["xy"][0]) > 5e-4 or abs(xy[1] - MOUNT["xy"][1]) > 5e-4:
   716	            bad.append(f"at ({xy[0]:.3f}, {xy[1]:.3f}), want {MOUNT['xy']}")
   717	        self.report("M3 hole", f"{drill[0]:.2f} mm", not bad,
   718	                    "; ".join(bad) if bad else
   719	                    f"{ref} unplated, no annular ring, at ({xy[0]:.2f}, {xy[1]:.2f}) "
   720	                    f"-- M3 clearance, ISO 273 medium")
   721	
   722	    def _copper_shapes(self):
   723	        """[(tag, shape)] for every piece of copper on the board, both faces.
   724	
   725	        Zone fills come back as SHAPE_POLY_SET, tracks/vias/pads as SHAPE; both
   726	        answer Collide(), which is all the caller needs.
   727	        """
   728	        out, zones = [], 0
   729	        for t in self.board.Tracks():
   730	            for layer in (pcbnew.F_Cu, pcbnew.B_Cu):
   731	                if not t.IsOnLayer(layer):
   732	                    continue
   733	                p = t.GetPosition()
   734	                out.append((f"{t.GetNetname() or '<none>'}@"
   735	                            f"({mm(p.x - ORG.x):.2f},{mm(p.y - ORG.y):.2f})",
   736	                            t.GetEffectiveShape(layer)))
   737	        for fp in self.board.Footprints():
   738	            for p in fp.Pads():
   739	                if p.GetAttribute() == pcbnew.PAD_ATTRIB_NPTH:
   740	                    continue     # a hole is not copper
   741	                for layer in (pcbnew.F_Cu, pcbnew.B_Cu):
   742	                    if not p.IsOnLayer(layer):
   743	                        continue
   744	                    out.append((f"{fp.GetReference()}.{p.GetNumber()}",
   745	                                p.GetEffectiveShape(layer)))
   746	        for z in self.board.Zones():
   747	            for layer in (pcbnew.F_Cu, pcbnew.B_Cu):
   748	                if not z.IsOnLayer(layer):
   749	                    continue
   750	                zones += 1
   751	                out.append((f"zone {z.GetNetname()}", z.GetFilledPolysList(layer)))
   752	        return out, zones
   753	
   754	    def mount_keepout(self):
   755	        """How far the copper stands back from the M3 screw, MEASURED.
   756	
   757	        The screw goes into the heatsink, so it sits at the mounting surface's
   758	        potential.  The bottom island is bare TPAD copper that floats at whatever
   759	        the shunt floats at, separated from that surface only by the user's
   760	        thermal interface.  Copper under the screw head, or copper reaching the
   761	        hole wall, bonds the two and silently bypasses the only isolation this
   762	        board has -- while DRC stays green, because a 3.2 mm hole 0.3 mm from a
   763	        pour breaks no rule it knows about.
   764	
   765	        Reported as the largest copper-free radius about the hole centre, found
   766	        by bisection.  That number moves monotonically as the geometry gets
   767	        worse; a boolean "does anything collide" would not say how close it came.
   768	        """
   769	        if not MOUNT:
   770	            return
   771	        shapes, zones = self._copper_shapes()
   772	        # Absence of evidence: a scan that found no copper must not read as
   773	        # "nothing was too close".
   774	        if len(shapes) < 2 or zones == 0:
   775	            self.report("M3 keep-out", "n/a", False,
   776	                        f"found {len(shapes)} copper items and {zones} zone fills -- "
   777	                        f"nothing to measure against, so this check verified nothing")
   778	            return
   779	        ctr = self._hole_centre()
   780	        if ctr is None:
   781	            self.report("M3 keep-out", "n/a", False,
   782	                        "no single unplated hole on the board to measure from")
   783	            return
   784	
   785	        def hit(r_mm):
   786	            c = pcbnew.SHAPE_CIRCLE(ctr, pcbnew.FromMM(max(r_mm, 1e-4)))
   787	            for tag, s in shapes:
   788	                if s.Collide(c, 0):
   789	                    return tag
   790	            return None
   791	
   792	        want = MOUNT["clear_d"] / 2.0
   793	        lo, hi, where = 0.0, 12.0, hit(12.0)
   794	        if where is None:
   795	            self.report("M3 keep-out", "n/a", False,
   796	                        "no copper within 12 mm of the hole in either direction -- "
   797	                        "the bisection has no bracket and measured nothing")
   798	            return
   799	        for _ in range(40):
   800	            mid = (lo + hi) / 2.0
   801	            tag = hit(mid)
   802	            if tag:
   803	                hi, where = mid, tag
   804	            else:
   805	                lo = mid
   806	        self.report("M3 keep-out", f"{lo:.3f} mm", lo >= want,
   807	                    f"copper-free radius about the hole; needs >= {want} mm "
   808	                    f"({MOUNT['clear_d']} mm keep-out for a {MOUNT['head_d']} mm "
   809	                    f"DIN 912 head). Nearest copper: {where}. That leaves "
   810	                    f"{lo - MOUNT['drill'] / 2.0:.2f} mm from the hole WALL to copper, "
   811	                    f"which is the TPAD-to-screw creepage")
   812	
   813	    def _disc(self, ctr, r_mm, n=96):
   814	        poly = pcbnew.SHAPE_POLY_SET()
   815	        poly.NewOutline()
   816	        for i in range(n):
   817	            a = 2 * math.pi * i / n
   818	            poly.Append(int(ctr.x + pcbnew.FromMM(r_mm) * math.cos(a)),
   819	                        int(ctr.y + pcbnew.FromMM(r_mm) * math.sin(a)))
   820	        return poly
   821	
   822	    def mount_head_seat(self):
   823	        """The screw head must land entirely on board, not half over the edge.
   824	
   825	        Measured as the largest disc centred on the hole that fits inside the
   826	        real Edge_Cuts outline -- so trimming the tab, or moving the hole toward
   827	        an edge, walks this number down instead of tripping a threshold nothing
   828	        watches.  A head hanging over the edge cocks the screw and puts the
   829	        clamping load on one side of the board, which for a 0.6 mm laminate
   830	        pressed against a heatsink is the whole mechanism failing quietly.
   831	        """
   832	        if not MOUNT:
   833	            return
   834	        ctr = self._hole_centre()
   835	        if ctr is None:
   836	            self.report("M3 head seat", "n/a", False,
   837	                        "no single unplated hole on the board to seat a head on")
   838	            return
   839	        outline = pcbnew.SHAPE_POLY_SET()
   840	        if not self.board.GetBoardPolygonOutlines(outline) or outline.OutlineCount() == 0:
   841	            self.report("M3 head seat", "n/a", False,
   842	                        "board outline did not resolve to a polygon -- nothing to "
   843	                        "seat the head against")
   844	            return
   845	
   846	        def fits(r_mm):
   847	            over = self._disc(ctr, r_mm)
   848	            over.BooleanSubtract(outline)
   849	            return mm(mm(over.Area())) <= 1e-3
   850	
   851	        if not fits(MOUNT["drill"] / 2.0):
   852	            self.report("M3 head seat", "0.00 mm", False,
   853	                        "the hole itself is not fully inside the board outline")
   854	            return
   855	        lo, hi = MOUNT["drill"] / 2.0, 12.0
   856	        for _ in range(30):
   857	            mid = (lo + hi) / 2.0
   858	            if fits(mid):
   859	                lo = mid
   860	            else:
   861	                hi = mid
   862	        self.report("M3 head seat", f"{2 * lo:.2f} mm", 2 * lo >= MOUNT["head_d"],
   863	                    f"largest head that seats fully on the board; needs >= "
   864	                    f"{MOUNT['head_d']} mm (DIN 912 cap). A DIN 125 washer is 7.0 mm "
   865	                    f"and is NOT assumed -- see variants.py")
   866	
   867	    def run_quiet(self):
   868	        self.lines = []
   869	        self.fails = []
   870	        self._checks()
   871	        return self.fails
   872	
   873	    def run(self):
   874	        self._checks()
   875	        print("\n".join(self.lines))
   876	        return self.fails
   877	
