   438	
   439	## Review — 2026-08-07
   440	
   441	Three independent reviews (datasheet compliance, layout/electrical, guards and
   442	generators). Every finding below was re-verified here before acting on it;
   443	where a reviewer was right about the defect and wrong about the number, both
   444	are recorded.
   445	
   446	### Fixed
   447	
   448	| # | finding | status |
   449	|---|---|---|
   450	| 1 | **Address was wrong: ADD0→SDA is 0x4A, not 0x4B** (Table 7-2, p.21). DESIGN.md cited Table 5-1, which contains no addresses at all. The wrong value was **silkscreened on the board**. | fixed everywhere incl. silk |
   451	| 2 | **BOM merged R3+R4** into one row with `DNP = "no,yes"`. A fab places both → SDA shorted to V+ through 2 × 0 Ω; the probe cannot ACK and the host drives a short. ERC/DRC cannot see it. | BOM now ungrouped |
   452	| 3 | **Board thickness was 1.6 mm.** `write_stackup()` spliced `(setup …)` but never touched `(general (thickness …))`, which pcbnew wrote from its 1.6 default — and that is the field kicad-cli copies into `.gbrjob` as `BoardThickness`. The fab would have built 1.6 mm laminate. | fixed + guarded |
   453	| 4 | **`stackup_present()` was a presence proxy** — it grepped for `'(stackup'` and `ENIG` and printed "0.6 mm" without ever reading a number. It passed the 1.6 mm board. | now parses and compares thickness, layer sum, copper count, finish |
   454	| 5 | **EP→island thermal path omitted the copper.** Claimed 10.6 K/W from six barrels; the vias sit 0.6–1.3 mm north of the EP land and the 1.0 mm × 0.6 mm feed stub alone is 43 K/W. | `audit.py` now walks the real copper graph: **34 K/W**. (Reviewer's hand estimate was ~65 K/W — right about the omission, wrong about the magnitude, because it summed each via's feed in series instead of as a parallel network.) |
   455	| 6 | **`k = 0.76` was unsound in two directions** — wrong down-path, and RθJA is a JEDEC board-in-air composite that double-counts a board. | no k is claimed any more; calibrate the built probe |
   456	| 7 | **`_mask_area()` measured bounding boxes of drawings** — position-, copper- and overlap-blind. Apertures moved off the island entirely still reported 50.2 mm². | now intersects apertures with the real B.Cu fill: **46.5 mm²** |
   457	| 8 | **`gen_fp.py` guards were bare `assert`** — deleted by `python3 -O`, which then writes both footprints and exits 0. | now `raise` |
   458	| 9 | §10.1's **rigid-vs-flexible Note** — the most adverse sentence in the datasheet on this board's headline departure — was not quoted. | quoted, in full, in the departure section |
   459	| 10 | Missing host obligations: **pullups > 2 kΩ** (§8.2.2.2), **8 averages / 1 Hz and VIL ≤ 0.05·V+, VIH ≥ 0.95·V+** for the ±0.1 °C figure (§6.5), **1.8 V** supply floor above 70 °C (§6.3). | added to build notes and the connector table |
